# Commit:  831623f2965e34554304caabfc3a1e4e3741db1f (tag 144.0.7559.132)
# License: BSD-3-Clause (see CREDITS.md)
# Changes: regenerated against v8 at the DEPS pin for Chromium 151.0.7922.137,
#          v8_revision 00c2754b59cf5f79b323950c63b07cfb1a8377d4. The header hunk and the
#          messageAdded hunk applied unchanged (the latter at +27); addBindings needed rebuilding,
#          because 151's v8 added `int contextGroupId` / `int contextId` locals and a re-entrancy
#          check -- if (!m_inspector->getContext(contextGroupId, contextId)) return; -- inside both
#          loops.
#
#          Those two locals cannot stay live above the early return the way the 144 patch leaves
#          `contextName` live: -Wunused-variable fires for an int and not for a String16, whose
#          constructor and destructor are non-trivial. So they are commented out with the rest of
#          the body and only contextName remains above `return;`, which is exactly the shape the
#          144 patch has.
#
# This is the only Tier 1 patch that touches v8, a DEPS-managed separate repository.
#
# Suppresses the classic Runtime.enable CDP tell. With a debugger attached, serialising a console
# message reads Error.prototype.stack, so a page can plant a getter on `stack`, call console.debug,
# and learn that something is inspecting it. The patch stops V8RuntimeAgentImpl from reporting
# console messages, stops it from installing Runtime bindings, and makes enabled() always return
# false.
#
# Measured 2026-08-21 by attaching a CDP client, calling Runtime.enable and watching what the
# inspector volunteers -- control binary vs this build:
#
#                              control   patched
#   Runtime.evaluate works       true      true     (the baseline harness is unaffected)
#   executionContextCreated       1         1       (enable() reports contexts directly)
#   consoleAPICalled              1         0       <- the patch working
#   in-page Error#stack tell      0         0
#
# So it does close the channel: with a debugger attached the inspector no longer forwards the page's
# console output, and object serialisation is what the classic probe depends on. But that probe --
# plant a getter on an Error's stack, console.log it, see whether the getter fires -- reads 0 on the
# UNPATCHED 151 too, so this particular tell was already inert upstream. Recorded rather than
# claimed: see Veil/docs/MIGRATION-UNGOOGLED.md 5.1p.
#
# Cost: consoleAPICalled going to 0 means an attached DevTools shows nothing the page logs. Veil
# consumes no CDP console events today (nothing in the repo subscribes to consoleAPICalled), so
# nothing here breaks, but any future automation that reads page logs would.
#
# The detection baseline cannot see this: the harness itself drives the browser over CDP, and it
# never calls Runtime.enable (its client has a five-method allowlist). Verified out of band instead.
#
